# ADR-320 PostgreSQL trigger evaluation

Evaluated on 2026-08-23 after ADR-318 qualified the initial SLOs and ADR-319
accepted the initial product policy.

| Trigger | Evidence | Met |
|---|---|---|
| SQLite cannot sustain 2 commits/s | 44.424 commits/s, 100/100 durable rows | No |
| Multiple API writer hosts required | Single writer host remains approved | No |
| Database-enforced RLS required | No approved RLS requirement | No |
| HA or PITR required | Initial encrypted backup and 4-hour RTO remain approved | No |
| Distributed job claiming required | No approved distributed-worker requirement | No |

Decision: **DEFERRED**. The PostgreSQL adapter, JDBC driver, RLS, distributed
claims, HA/PITR, and dual-write paths remain absent. The conditional
post-migration storage-contract and replay checks do not run until a trigger is
approved; their required offline sequence is documented in
`docs/persistence/postgresql-trigger.md`.
